        "cover, soft rock, ballad, emotional, nostalgic, male vocal, piano, drums, clarinet, oboe. heartfelt song, stronger in the choruses.  ",
        "[intro]\n\n\n[Verse]\nThere's people that have put us down\npeople that have given us crowns\nand people that have passed in the night\nsongs I could have sung to you\nfeelings they began with you\nand its no lie that you make things right\nI could make love to you all night\nI could make love to you til light\nDancing our way to the morning\nI need you, and you need me\nand that's the way it seems to be\ntouching on eternity\n\n[Chorus] \nMy love takes over the train\nlooking out to you again\nSee you, feel you\nwe've seen alice through the looking glass\ngive you names and make you laugh\nJoin me, on the heart train.\n\n\n[Verse]\nI take a glance through our history\nfriends we've had, friends we've been\nsometimes I wonder but I think it's been alright.\nwe met at schoool, I played the fool\nyou the princess, broke no rules\nbut I've seen you in a different light\ntimes around us change\ninnocence may turn to blame\nits so hard to keep our dreams alive\nbut someday we will understand\nwhy we met in this strange land\nstruggling, fighting to survive\n\n[Chorus]\nMy love takes over the train\nlooking out to you again\nfeel you, see you\nwe've seen alice through the looking glass\nyou give me names and make me laugh\njoin me, on the heart train.\n\n[drop]\n\n[Verse]\nThis is our time, this is our time\nthis is what I give to you\nwe're heading for a moment\nthe end of our lives\nI know it and it makes me want to cry\nI dont want to die, I dont want to say goodbye\nI know there's another road to try\nIt's what I'm trying to say to you\ndon't let our enemies take us too\nhelp me find the way to defeat their lies.\n\n[Chorus]\nMy love takes over the train\nlooking out to you again\nfeel you, need you\nwe've seen alice through the looking glass\ngive you names and make you laugh\nfeel you, to be with you.\n\n[Chorus]\nMy love takes over the train\nlooking out to you again\nSee you, feel you.\nwe've seen smokey rooms and whisky days\nliving in such strange ways\njoin me, on the heart train.\n\n",
        233795100990875,
